rginia approached the window, opening it. A tall figure stood below in the alley, stooping down to pick up a handful of sand. [3023] Virginia's heart raced faster. Soon, she recognized the broad, muscular silhouette as that of Packard. [3024] \"I'm here,\" she whispered, \"What is it?\" [3025] It was strange for Packard to throw sand at her window at this hour. [3026] \"What is it?\" she asked impatiently. [3027] \"The master sent me,\" Boris's voice was low but clear. \"He sent me to fetch you.\" [3028] He spoke deliberately. [3029] \"To fetch me?\" [3030] \"Yes, he wants me to bring you to him. Here's a note, I'll toss it up to you.\" [3031] Virginia stepped back a little, and a note pressed down by a pebble fell at her feet. She opened the note, which read:\n[3032] Dear (Anthony wrote), I am in danger and am trying to escape. Will you believe me and come to me? [3033] Virginia stood there motionless for two minutes, reading and rereading the short message. [3034] She looked up, taking in the luxurious furnishings of the bedroom around her, feeling as if everything had changed. [3035] Then, she peered out the window again. [3036] \"What should I do?\" she asked. [3037] \"The detectives are on the other side of the villa, outside the conference room. You go downstairs and come out through the side door. I'll be waiting there, and I'll bring the car to the curb.\" [3038] Virginia nodded, quickly changing out of her dress and into a light yellow knit sweater, and donning a light yellow leather cap. [3039] She then wrote a short note, leaving it for Bunder, and pinned it to the needle cushion. [3040] She crept downstairs, unlocked the side door's latch. She hesitated for a moment, bravely tossing her head, much like her ancestors did when joining the Crusaders, and then stepped out. [3041] Chapter 26, October 13\n[3042] On October 13, Tuesday, at 10 a.m., Anthony Ked walked into the Hotel Harijgi to see Baron Lothrop Loyd, who was staying in a suite here. [3043] After