l?\" [1412] The big financier nodded. [1413] \"What he means is that, as a candidate for the throne of Hesse-Slav, he would be more popular than Prince Michael, because of his modern and enlightened ideas, and his early support for democratic and republican ideals. If the American consortium could support him, he would grant them a concession in return.\" [1414] At this point, Balthazar had forgotten his habit of keeping his emotions in check and whistled a long, low whistle. [1415] \"So that's it,\" he murmured. \"On the other hand, the monarchists support Prince Michael. But you think you have the upper hand. And then this happened.\" [1416] \"You don't think\u2026\" George said. [1417] \"It's a big deal,\" the sheriff said. \"That's what Mr. Isakov said. A big deal, must be a very big deal.\" [1418] \"There will always be underhanded situations,\" Isakov said calmly. \"Now, Wall Street has the upper hand. But we haven't settled our differences yet. Sheriff, if you want to serve your country, find the killer of Prince Michael.\" [1419] \"There's one thing that strikes me as suspicious,\" George interjected. \"Why didn't Captain Androidsi come with the prince yesterday?\" [1420] \"I've already looked into it,\" Balthazar said. \"It's quite simple. He stayed in the city to meet a young lady for Prince Michael to arrange a date for the following weekend. The baron disapproves of this, believing it to be unwise at this stage. So the prince had to do it secretly. He, you could say, is quite a free-spirited young man.\" [1421] \"Probably,\" said George stiffly. \"Ah, probably.\" [1422] \"There's one more thing we need to keep in mind,\" Bartel hesitated. \"Victor King should be in Britain right now.\" [1423] \"Victor King?\" Ramecs furrowed his brow, trying to recall the name. [1424] \"That infamous French con artist, sir. The French security agency has warned us.\" [1425] \"Oh,\" said Ramecs. \"I remember now. The jewel thief, right? What? The\u2026\"\n[1426] Bartlett 