ne through another door to the rooms downstairs, the one on the corridor. I didn't hear him go out. Maybe I was drugged. I'm a negligent servant. My master is awake, and I'm sleeping. I should be damned.\" [1465] George stared at him intently, somewhat dazed. [1466] \"You have a lot of affection for your master?\" Batter asked, keeping a close eye on the other's movements. [1467] Baxter's face contorted with pain. He struggled to speak twice before his voice became shrill with emotion. [1468] \"British police, I tell you, I would die for him. Now he's dead, and I'm still alive, and if I don't avenge him, I'll die with my eyes closed and never find peace. I'll hunt down the murderer like a hound, and once I find him... Ah!\" He spoke with fire in his eyes. [1469] Suddenly, he pulled a large knife from his coat and waved it in the air. \"I won't kill him right away. No, I'll cut off his nose first, then chop off his ears, and gouge out his eyes. Then, I'll stab him in the heart with this knife!\" [1470] He turned and quickly put the knife back in its place, leaving the room. George stared intently at the door, which was now closed, and his already protruding eyes seemed ready to burst from their sockets. [1471] \"A true Hessian,\" he muttered. [1472] \"A savage race, a bunch of bandits,\" Balthar the constable alertly stood up. [1473] \"Either he's truly devoted or he's just putting on a show,\" he commented. \"If it's the former, God help the killer when he's caught.\" [1474] Chapter 15: The Stranger from France\n[1475] Virginia and Anthony walked side by side along the path to the lake. After leaving the room, neither of them spoke for a few minutes until Virginia finally broke the silence with a giggle. [1476] \"Hey,\" she said, \"wasn't that scary? I have a lot to tell you and a lot to ask, but I don't know where to start. First, in a low voice, \"how did you handle the body? It sounds terrifying, and I never thought I'd be involved in a crime.\" [1477] \"It's new