e gunshots too.\" [1515] \"If so, they haven't said anything about it today. I heard from Inspector Bartlett that no one in the house heard gunshots. That's my only lead, not very reliable, but I'm still going to pursue it.\" [1516] \"It's really strange,\" Virginia pondered. [1517] They walked to the boathouse by the lake, leaning against the wall and talking. [1518] \"Let's go over everything now,\" Anthony said, \"let's take our time and row out on the lake so that the police, the American guests, and the gossiping maid can't overhear us.\" [1519] \"I heard some things from the Earl of Carringham,\" Virginia said, \"but not much. Tell me, are you Anthony Kidd or Jimmy McGregor?\" [1520] So, Anthony recounted the story he had told earlier, but with a slight difference in what he said to Virginia. From six weeks ago until he unexpectedly recognized the \"Mr. Holmes\" figure. [1521] \"By the way, Mrs. Rue,\" he said finally. \"I haven't thanked you yet for lying about me being your old friend.\" [1522] \"You are my old friend, aren't you?\" Virginia exclaimed. \"You don't think I'd have pushed the body on you and then pretend we're just acquaintances when we meet again, do you? I'm not that kind of person.\" She paused and then continued, \"You know, there's one thing that really surprises me. I had no idea that the memoir had such an unexpected mystery.\" [1523] \"You're right,\" Anthony agreed. \"There's one thing I want to ask you.\" [1524] \"What is it?\" [1525] \"When I mentioned Jimmy McGregor's name to you yesterday on Pound Street, why did you seem so surprised? Had you heard of him before?\" [1526] \"Sherlock Holmes, I have heard of him. George, my cousin George Roxborough, came to me one day and talked about a bunch of nonsense. He wanted me to come here and try to seduce this McGregor into giving up the memoir. Of course, he didn't say it like that. He talked about British ladies and all that useless stuff, but his intentions were clear. It's only poor ol