ould answer, he picked up the box and moved it to the side of the row of trees. He bent down and something flashed in his hand, and the lock of the box was opened. [2495] He spoke a sentence, but his voice was different from before, fast and commanding:\n[2496] \"The car will be here soon,\" he said. \"Is it here yet?\" [2497] Virginia turned around to look at the villa. [2498] \"No.\" [2499] \"Good.\" [2500] He quickly took out the contents of the box one by one: bottles with gold lids, silk pajamas, various socks. Suddenly, he stiffened. He grabbed a package that looked like silk lingerie and quickly opened it. [2501] Bill couldn't help but let out a soft \"Oh\" as he saw a heavy-looking handgun in the center of the package. [2502] \"I hear the horn,\" Virginia said. [2503] Lemon quickly organized the suitcase, wrapped the gun in his silk handkerchief, and put it in his pocket. Then he locked the suitcase with a \"click\" and turned to Bill:\n[2504] \"Take this, you and the lady. Stop the car and tell them the suitcase fell out of the luggage compartment. Don't mention me.\" [2505] Bill quickly walked down the driveway as the Lancaster sedan approached the turn, with Eisakstein inside. The driver slowed down, and Bill waved the suitcase at him. [2506] \"This suitcase fell out of the trunk,\" he explained, \"We just happened to see it.\" [2507] He saw the financier's yellow face go blank, staring at him intently. Then, the car continued on its way. [2508] They turned around and found Lemmon standing there, triumphant, holding the handgun. [2509] \"Aha,\" he said, \"I've finally found it.\" [2510] Chapter XXII: The Red Signal\n[2511] Sheriff Bartlett was standing in the library of Weinberg College. [2512] George Roxbury sat at a desk piled high with papers, frowning and looking haughty. [2513] Sheriff Bartlett briefly reported the situation, and the rest of the conversation was dominated by George, with the sheriff interjecting only occasionally with a word or two. 